eally uh  highly resistant to careful toxin with  mic greater than 256  microgram per mill so  we wanted to know if these  multi-resistant  strains are clustering and what we did  together with york rao in stuttgart  we did a cluster analysis using the  the ir biotyper and you see here these  results of different  archobacter but bootslovery isolates  from our labs and on the right  side of the panel you see the resistance  susceptible or resistance and then  we did the analysis with the ir biotyper  and this revealed a clustering of the  multi-resistant  strains so the pun resistant strains  resistant to tetracyclines macrolides  and  fluoroquinolones they clustered here in  in one cluster as a ce1 and c2  cluster while the  tetracycline and macrolide resistant but  fluoroquinoline  fluoroquinolone susceptible strains say  clustered differently in in the  subcluster e  so this helped us uh we have a  collection of more than 220 acrobacter  butler restraints meanwhile and we have  dude we do not have the kappa  capacity currently to sequence them all  so this really helps us to pick the  strains  we use for whole genome sequencing to  find this viral lens  factors and resistance factors within  the echobacter community so this is  really helpful as a yeah kind of  pre analysis for  for next generation sequencing also  so uh to sum up uh for the ir biotype  version 3.0  this offers a possibility to connect the  multibiotyper to the ir biotyper this is  this really beautiful 3d  scatter plots which gives you  clouds of differently colored  pneumococcus capsule types or  salmonella o types  it has an improved graphical  user interface which is easy to use  an improved usability with easy  reporting for example as a pdf  run report you now have in the version  3.0 the full wave number range from  800 to 4000 nanometers of wavelength  and as i've shown you in detail you have  the possibilities who set these  classifiers for pneumococcal  serial grouping for salmonella ty